      "writtenOn": "2017-07-21T20:32:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why would you not want to be thread safe?  Does the locking incur significant overhead for the cases where thread safety is unnecessary?\n\nWhy is locking necessary at all?  It is often not needed in go, where it is more idiomatic to try to only access an object from a single goroutine.",
      "revId": "e04f15a442a1a498f7095cbcb13a448f61cc5496",
