      "lineNbr": 126,
      "author": {
        "id": 1137668
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-07-22T02:29:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, it would have to lock at least 180,000 times, and the current implementation runs in about 0.25 sec.\n\nYeah, there are two main cases where this gets used: one is when there\u0027s a thread-local copy being constructed in Finder.loadBytes (which is when we set threadsafe\u003dfalse), the other is where there\u0027s a static copy being modified in Finder.pollForStatResponses (which is when we set threadsafe\u003dtrue) . I could split it into two classes, one threadsafe and the other not, but it seemed to me like a lot of code duplication.\n\nWhat would you do differently than what Finder.pollForStatResponses does currently? With a single workers thread in pollForStatResponses, that works fine without any locks, but it seemed odd to limit the number of workers to 1 (and it runs slightly faster (2.2 sec on the first `find` (which is where this makes a difference)) to have 4 worker threads with locks than 1 worker thread without locks (4.7 sec on the first `find`))",
      "parentUuid": "e4768919_fed6e383",
      "revId": "e04f15a442a1a498f7095cbcb13a448f61cc5496",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
