      "writtenOn": "2017-07-22T02:29:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah it\u0027s 17MB in total, but split among 100 threads it\u0027s 170KB each, and each thread takes roughly 20ms to parse its block (the parsing is parallelized with the reading)\n\nThe gob decoding did run faster and did have a smaller file size, but most of the file was text anyway so I didn\u0027t notice a significant decrease in file size or in time to load the file. I didn\u0027t take exact measurements on (or implement fully) the gob performance since the json performance seemed pretty good to me.\n\n\nHow much time savings do you think is worth the switch from json to gob?",
      "parentUuid": "50f730f7_6bbb650d",
      "revId": "e04f15a442a1a498f7095cbcb13a448f61cc5496",
